{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3105-77f5-8869-4527b594c6fe","id":"01a1a58d-a4de-746c-8a76-71bed7f47000","idempotency_key":"974008c11ad8c3ff12e66af3bbed6bab42af6ceb0edb15a4e01a34634fb9cdbc","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T07:54:45Z","payload":{"note":"Schema v5 adds ai_events (stream_kind, stream_id, event_id, payload_json, created; PK on the first three) with append_ai_event/ai_events(after)/latest_ai_event_id in rbc-db, the id assigned by the store so two writers cannot reuse one. crates/ai/src/events.rs wraps it as EventLog over StreamKey::session / StreamKey::game with append, append_all, replay(after), latest and has_more; replay reconstructs AiEventPayload from the stored JSON. crates/ai/src/context_diff.rs diffs a stored context against a rebuilt one by section id and reports added/removed/changed with a sha256 per section, ignoring key order. Server: GET /api/ai/sessions/{id}/stream?after= returns Server-Sent Events, each with event: ai, id: <cursor> and the flattened AiEvent JSON, so EventSource reconnects via Last-Event-ID; the handler polls the stored log (stateless, so a late or reconnecting client sees the same stream), sends keep-alives and closes after ~2 minutes of silence. send_ai_turn now records its AgentLoop events through append_all after the turn finishes; replay/{seq} returns the ContextDiff instead of two hashes alone. Evidence: cargo test -p rbc-ai --all-features stream -> 9 tests (ordered replay with monotonic ids, reconnect returns only new events, ids keep counting after a reopen, sessions and matches keep separate sequences, empty stream, every payload shape round-trips, diff identical/drifted/removed). Also verified live against a mock provider: 13 events in order (turn_started, context_ready, usage, tool_call, tool_result, 6 content deltas, usage, turn_done), after=10 returned 11-13, /api/health reports schema 5.","target":"t-d0bf"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3105-77f5-8869-4527b594c6fe","id":"01a1a58e-95f2-74c6-b6c1-96df90282d4a","idempotency_key":"1848b69e792a608dcc9871f562f598afdcbe308775f721f2091d054f1b0e6e2d","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T07:55:47Z","payload":{"note":"Correction after closing: send_ai_turn records each event from the AgentLoop sink as it is emitted, not in one append_all at the end (commit after de1d4a7). Verified live: with a mock provider delaying 400ms per content delta, the stream delivered turn_started at 32.51, deltas at 33.02-35.02 and turn_done at 35.03, so a watching client sees the turn as it runs. The log is therefore also durable mid-turn.","target":"t-d0bf"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
